Body:
@peri4n are you experiencing this error?
```
Function tools with reasoning_effort are not supported for gpt-5.5 in /v1/chat/completions. Please use /v1/responses instead.
```
In opencode v1.3.16, [this pr](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/20272) fixes provider options for azure sdk. But it breaks the `/v1/chat/completions` method.

<hr>

Removing `reasoning_effort` from fetch body does solve this problem, but I am not sure this will be a good solution, since this is too much of custom logic for this specific provider. @rekram1-node 

[packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/754a1fb712e2b79c8786e27af58f7ae0c1e34d65/packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts#L1486)
```
// Strip openai itemId metadata following what codex does
if (
  (model.api.npm === "@ai-sdk/openai" || model.api.npm === "@ai-sdk/azure") &&
  opts.body &&
  opts.method === "POST"
) {
  const body = JSON.parse(opts.body as string)
  const keepIds = body.store === true
  let bodyChanged = false
  if (!keepIds && Array.isArray(body.input)) {
    for (const item of body.input) {
      if ("id" in item) {
        delete item.id
        bodyChanged = true
      }
    }
  }
  // Remove reasoning_effort for /v1/chat/completions
  if (options["useCompletionUrls"]) {
    delete body["reasoning_effort"]
    bodyChanged = true
  }
  if (bodyChanged) {
    opts.body = JSON.stringify(body)
  }
}
```

<hr>

For now, I would recommend sticking to a fix version of opencode if you are using azure with `/chat/completion` endpoint, since it is already mention in above reply that this azure deployment/completion endpoint being an old artifact with discontinue updates

I ran into this when selecting the European Claude Opus 4.6 model from OpenCode’s `/models` list with Amazon Bedrock.
The model shown/needed in Bedrock was:
```txt
eu.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1
```

but selecting it directly from the OpenCode model picker failed with:

```txt
undefined: The provided model identifier is invalid.
```

The workaround that fixed it was to define the model explicitly in the OpenCode config (`~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`) using a custom alias, and map that alias to the exact Bedrock model identifier:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "amazon-bedrock/claude-opus-4-6-eu",
  "provider": {
    "amazon-bedrock": {
      "options": {
        "region": "eu-west-1"
      },
      "models": {
        "claude-opus-4-6-eu": {
          "id": "eu.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1",
          "name": "Claude Opus 4.6 EU"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
